    "chunk_text": "Dated at the Office of the Commissioner General of Labour,Colombo, on this 16th day of July, 2025.\n\nEOG 08- 0060\n\nMy No.: IR/COM/04/2022/124.\n\nTHE INDUSTRIAL DISPUTES ACT, CHAPTER 131 OF THE LEGISLATIVE ENACTMENTS OF CEYLON(1956 REVISED EDITION)\n\nRevocation of Order under Section 4(1)\n\nMr. D.P.N.H. Mohotti, No. 32/2B, 7th Lane, Crow Island, Colombo 05.\n\nand\n\nVocational Training Authority of Sri Lanka, 354/2, 4th Floor, Nipunatha Piyasa, Elvitigala Mawatha, Narahenpita, Colombo 05.\n\nWas referred to Mr. A.B. Herath for settlement by arbitration.\n\n3AI \u0dd9\u0d9a\u0dcf\u0da7\u0dc3 \u0dd9\u0d9a\u0dcf\u0da7\u0dc3: (I): (I) \u0dd9\u0da1\u0daf\u0dba \u0dd9\u0da1\u0daf\u0dba \u2013 \u2013 \u027c \u0dbd\u0d82\u0d9a\u0dcf \u021d\u0da2\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dcf\u01e6\u01b5\u0d9a \u0dc3\u0db8\u0dcf\u0da2\u0dc0\u0dcf\u01cf \u0da2\u0db1\u0dbb\u0da2\u0dd9\u024f \u0d85\u01af \u026a\u0dd9\u0dc1\u0dc2 \u0d9c\u0dd0\u0dc3\u0178 \u0db4\u01b4\u0dba \u027c \u0dbd\u0d82\u0d9a\u0dcf \u021d\u0da2\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dcf\u01e6\u01b5\u0d9a \u0dc3\u0db8\u0dcf\u0da2\u0dc0\u0dcf\u01cf \u0da2\u0db1\u0dbb\u0da2\u0dd9\u024f \u0d85\u01af \u026a\u0dd9\u0dc1\u0dc2 \u0d9c\u0dd0\u0dc3\u0178 \u0db4\u01b4\u0dba \u2013 2025.08.05\u2013 2025.08.05\n\nP\u0d7a\u0d8b\u0d8d I: S\u0d7e\u0d7c. (I)P\u0d7a\u0d8b\u0d8d I: S\u0d7e\u0d7c. (I) \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 05.08.2025 \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 05.08.2025\n\nAND Whereas it is now deemed expedient that the said Order be revoked, due to Mr. A.B. Herath, the Arbitrator informing that he is resigning from this dispute, I, Dr. Anil Jayantha Fernando, Minister of Labour do hereby revoke the said Order and Further make Order that no proceedings be taken upon the said Order dated 25.03.2025.\n\nDr. ANIL JAYANTHA FERNANDO, Minister of Labour.\n\nColombo,31st July, 2025.\n\nEOG 08-0061/1\n\nMy No.: IR/COM/04/2022/124.\n\nTHE INDUSTRIAL DISPUTES ACT, CHAPTER 131 OF THE LEGISLATIVE ENACTMENTS OF CEYLON(1956 REVISED EDITION)\n\nOrder under Section 4(1)\n\nWHEREAS an industrial dispute in respect of the matter specified in the statement of the Commissioner General of Labour which accompanies this order exists between,\n\nMr. D.P.N.H. Mohotti, No. 32/2B, 7th Lane, Crow Island, Colombo 15.\n\nand\n\nVocational Training Authority of Sri Lanka, 354/2, 4th Floor, Nipunatha Piyasa, Elvitigala Mawatha, Narahenpita, Colombo 05."
