    "chunk_text": "1AI \u0dd9\u0d9a\u02a3\u0da7\u0dc3: (I) \u0dd9\u0da1\u0daf\u0dba \u2013 \u027c \u0dbd\u0d82\u0d9a\u0dcf \u021d\u0da2\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dcf\u01e6\u01b5\u0d9a \u0dc3\u0db8\u0dcf\u0da2\u0dc0\u0dcf\u01cf \u0da2\u0db1\u0dbb\u0da2\u0dd9\u024f \u0d85\u01af \u026a\u0dd9\u0dc1\u0dc2 \u0d9c\u0dd0\u0dc3\u0178 \u0db4\u01b4\u0dba \u2013 2025.08.12PART I: SEC. (I) \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 12.08.2025\n\n\u027c \u0dbd\u0d82\u0d9a\u0dcf \u021d\u0da2\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dcf\u01e6\u01b5\u0d9a \u0dc3\u0db8\u0dcf\u0da2\u0dc0\u0dcf\u01cf \u0da2\u0db1\u0dbb\u0da2\u0dd9\u024f \u0d9c\u0dd0\u0dc3\u0178 \u0db4\u01b4\u0dba\n\n\u0d85\u01af \u026a\u0dd9\u0dc1\u0dc2The Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\nEXTRAORDINARY\n\n\u0d85\u0d82\u0d9a 2449/12 \u2013 2025 \u0d85\u0dd9\u0d9c\u02a4\u0dc3\u0dca\u01b1 \u0db8\u0dc3 12 \u0dc0\u0dd0\u01e7 \u0d85\u0d9f\u0dc4\u025e\u0dc0\u0dcf\u0daf\u0dcf \u2013 2025.08.12\n\nNo. 2449/12 \u2013 TUESDAY, AUGUST 12, 2025\n\n(Published by Authority)\n\nPART I: SECTION (I) \u2013 GENERAL\n\nGovernment Noti\ufb01cations\n\nESALA FESTIVAL OF MAHIYANGANAYA \u2013 2025\n\nBY virtue of the powers vested in me by the Transfer of Powers (Divisional Secretaries) Act, No. 58 of 1992, and according to the regulations in terms of the provisions of the Chapter 362 of Pilgrimages Ordinance published in Government Gazette No. 9902 of 10th September, 1948, Gazette No. 10283 of 17th August, 1951, Gazette No. 14778 of 25th March, 1995 and Gazette No. 14752 of 09th June, 1967, I, Wickramanayake Wimansa Senevirathne the Divisional Secretary of Mahiyanganaya/the o\ufb03 cer-in-charge of the camp area, do hereby inform the following orders shall be in force with regard to the camp of Mahiyanganaya Esala Festival 2025.\n\n1. It is announced that Mahiyanganaya Esala Festival will be commenced on the 25th August, 2025 by \u201cKapsituweema\u201d ceremony and the closure of the event will be marked by \u201cDiya Kepeema\u201d Ceremony on the 08th September, 2025.\n\n2. The camping area for abode of pilgrims shall be the land demarcated from the 37th Mile Post of Mahiyanganaya -Bibila Main Road up to the 2/39 culvert in front of Mahiyanganaya National School, the front area of Villu Wewa Road and the area of land bounded by the lanes called \u201cGangawata Veediya\u201d \u201cAngmedilla Veediya\u201d and \u201cDevala Veediya\u201d which approaches the clock tower from the front of Mahiyanganaya Hospital.\n\n3. It is hereby prohibited cooking meals or do selling in or around the courtyards of \u201cSthupa Maluwa\u201d, \u201cBo Maluwa\u201d and \u201cDevala Premises\u201d.\n\n1A \u2013 G 045094 \u2013 14 (08/2025)"
