    "chunk_size_bytes": 1809,
    "chunk_text": "7. The area ahead of 10ft. from the water drain of both sides of Dutugemunu Street, Meda Mawatha, Ammedilla Road, Badulla-Mahiyanganaya Main Road, Bodimaluwa Mawatha and the road in front of the \u201cSangawasa (Bikku abode), that is noticed as the route of perahera by the \u201cBasnayaka Nilame\u201d and Ven. Chief Incumbent, is reserved for business purposes.\n\n9. Except as permitted in statement 04, 05 and 06 mentioned above, establishing temporary stalls or selling items in mobile stalls within the camp area or establishing temporary sheds other than the stalls already built on the two sides of \u201cGangawata Road\u201d is entirely prohibited.\n\n10. Parking of private vehicles on the main street is hereby prohibited.\n\n11. No person shall enter any type of vehicle into the camp area including bicycles and bullock carts without a permit issued by Divisional Secretary/the o\ufb03 cer-in-charge of the camp or any other authorized person by him.\n\n12. No person shall enter any motor vehicle into the camp via the main access road to \u201cPooja Bhoomi\u201d by the side of the \u201cWahalkada\u201d (Vestibule) which faces Mahiyanganaya-Bibila main road, Villuwa Wewa road, the access road by the side of the \u201cMakara Thorana\u201d, the road running close to the clock tower situated in front of the hospital and the road close to 2/39 culvert near Mahiyanganaya National School unless permit is obtained.\n\n13. Notice will be published by me on the procedure of leasing the parcels of land for business purpose within the camp area.\n\n14. All the temporary constructions in the leased out commercial lands shall comply with the speci\ufb01 cations made by the Medical O\ufb03 cer in Health of Mahiyanganaya.\n\n15. 01 or 02 mobile toilets adjacent to each boutique will have to be made available for the use of pilgrims, if ordered by me."
