    "chunk_text": "14. All the temporary constructions in the leased out commercial lands shall comply with the speci\ufb01 cations made by the Medical O\ufb03 cer in Health of Mahiyanganaya.\n\n15. 01 or 02 mobile toilets adjacent to each boutique will have to be made available for the use of pilgrims, if ordered by me.\n\n17. It is prohibited to construct any permanent or temporary building within camp area unless a license has been obtained from me.\n\n3AI \u0dd9\u0d9a\u02a3\u0da7\u0dc3: (I) \u0dd9\u0da1\u0daf\u0dba \u2013 \u027c \u0dbd\u0d82\u0d9a\u0dcf \u021d\u0da2\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dcf\u01e6\u01b5\u0d9a \u0dc3\u0db8\u0dcf\u0da2\u0dc0\u0dcf\u01cf \u0da2\u0db1\u0dbb\u0da2\u0dd9\u024f \u0d85\u01af \u026a\u0dd9\u0dc1\u0dc2 \u0d9c\u0dd0\u0dc3\u0178 \u0db4\u01b4\u0dba \u2013 2025.08.12PART I: SEC. (I) \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 12.08.2025\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA.\n\n18. No person shall without the previous sanction of the Divisional Secretary/O\ufb03 cer-in-Charge of camp construct any shed or any sort of building or extend any building, so as to encroach any land used or set apart for use as a street or any land forming the banks of a river within the camp area.\n\n19. Reserving seats under charges to watch the Perahera is strictly prohibited.\n\n20. Construction of temporary stalls along Badulla - Mahiyanganaya main road in-between the Zonal Education O\ufb03 ce and the new Covid Diagnostic Laboratory is strictly prohibited.\n\n21. Vehicle Parking Sites.-\n\n(i) the vehicle park reserved for the \u201cPooja Bhoomi\u201d (the piece of land in front of the hospital)\n\n(ii) The piece of land situated to the left of \u201cSirisangabo Pre-School\u201d and \u201cMakara Thorana\u201d and the area extending from there to \u201cBo Maluwa Veediya\u201d.\n\n(iii) The triangular piece of land in between the Villuwa Wewa road and Mahiyanganaya-Bibila road is allocated for parking passenger transport buses.\n\n22. It is prohibited to tie elephants and tuskers for the Perahera along the Mahaweli river bank of \u201cGangawata Veediya\u201d in day or night.\n\nConstitution 15\n\n(a) Firing of any sort of crackers is strictly prohibited within the camp area."
