    "chunk_text": "22. It is prohibited to tie elephants and tuskers for the Perahera along the Mahaweli river bank of \u201cGangawata Veediya\u201d in day or night.\n\nConstitution 15\n\n(a) Firing of any sort of crackers is strictly prohibited within the camp area.\n\nW. W\u0d82\u0d86\u0d7a\u0d87\u0d8c\u0d7a S\u0d7e\u0d87\u0d7e\u0d8f\u0d82\u0d8b\u0d7a\u0d8d\u0d81\u0d87\u0d7e, Divisional Secretary, Mahiyanganaya.\n\nMAHIYANGANAYA ESALA FESTIVAL \u2013 2025\n\nAccording to the regulations in terms of the provisions of the Chapter 362 of Pilgrimages Ordinance published in Government Gazette No. 9902 of 10th September, 1948, Gazette No. 10283 of 17th August, 1951, Gazette No. 14778 of 25th March, 1995 and Gazette No. 14752 of 09th June, 1967, and the transfer of powers Act (Divisional Secretaries), No. 58 of 1992, I, Wickramanayake Wimansa Senevirathne the Divisional Secretary of Mahiyanganaya/the o\ufb03 cer-in-charge of the camp, do hereby notify that the following places are allocated for the purpose of distributing and selling of food items among the pilgrims.\n\n(a) The permanent buildings in between the 37th Km and 2/39 culvert in front of the National School along Mahiyanganaya-Bibila road.\n\n(b) Temporary buildings constructed on a permit issued by me,within the allocated ground for abode of pilgrims inside the camp area.\n\nIt is prohibited any other place or land, within the camping areas except speci\ufb01 ed in the above.\n\nW. W\u0d82\u0d86\u0d7a\u0d87\u0d8c\u0d7a S\u0d7e\u0d87\u0d7e\u0d8f\u0d82\u0d8b\u0d7a\u0d8d\u0d81\u0d87\u0d7e, Divisional Secretary, Mahiyanganaya.At Mahiyanganaya District Secretariat,05th August, 2025.\n\nEOG 08 \u2013 0100"
